    {
      "@id": "concept:australian-capital-territory-planning-and-land-management-amendment-act-2018-sch-1-sec-46",
      "@type": "cml:Concept",
      "skos:prefLabel": "46 Functions of Chief Executive",
      "cml:realizedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/australian-capital-territory-planning-and-land-management-amendment-act-2018#sch-1-sec-46"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:schemaVersion": "2",
      "cml:proposedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml"
      },
      "prov:wasDerivedFrom": {
        "@id": "australian-capital-territory-planning-and-land-management-amendment-act-2018.pdf"
      },
      "dc:source": "australian-capital-territory-planning-and-land-management-amendment-act-2018.pdf, p.8",
      "values:originalText": "(1) The Chief Executive has the responsibility of managing the affairs\nof the Authority.\n\n(2) The Authority may give written directions to the Chief Executive\nabout the management of the Authority’s affairs.\n\n(3) The Chief Executive must comply with a direction under\nsubsection (2).\n\n(4) Subsection (3) does not apply to the extent that the direction relates\nto the Chief Executive’s performance of functions or exercise of\npowers under the Public Service Act 1999.\n\n(5) A direction under subsection (2) is not a legislative instrument.\n\nGovernance arrangements  Schedule 1\nSaving and transitional provisions  Part 2\n\nNo. 32, 2018\nAustralian Capital Territory (Planning and Land Management)\nAmendment Act 2018",
      "skos:definition": "(1) The Chief Executive has the responsibility of managing the affairs\nof the Authority.\n\n(2) The Authority may give written directions to the Chief Executive\nabout the management of the Authority’s affairs.\n\n(3) The Chief Executive must comply with a direction under\nsubsection (2).\n\n(4) Subsection (3) does not apply to the extent that the direction relates\nto the Chief Executive’s performance of functions or exercise of\npowers under the Public Service Act 1999.\n\n(5) A direction under subsection (2) is not a legislative instrument.\n\nGovernance arrangements  Schedule 1\nSaving and transitional provisions  Part 2\n\nNo. 32, 2018\nAustralian Capital Territory (Planning and Land Management)\nAmendment Act 2018",
      "cml:hasPart": [
